# 📘 Complete Guide: PostgreSQL + pgvector Setup (Step-by-Step)

---

## 🧱 1. Install PostgreSQL

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install postgresql postgresql-contrib
```

👉 Installs PostgreSQL server and basic tools.

---

## 🔐 2. Fix Authentication (Reset Password)

### Edit config file:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/postgresql/16/main/pg_hba.conf
```

### Change:

```text
local   all             postgres                                md5
```

👉 To:

```text
local   all             postgres                                trust
```

### Restart:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart postgresql
```

### Login without password:

```bash
sudo -i -u postgres
psql
```

### Set password:

```sql
ALTER USER postgres WITH PASSWORD 'postgres';
```

### Exit:

```sql
\q
exit
```

### Revert back to secure mode:

```text
local   all             postgres                                md5
```

Restart again:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart postgresql
```

---

## 🏗️ 3. Create User & Database

### Login:

```bash
psql -U postgres -h localhost
```

### Create user:

```sql
CREATE USER langchain WITH PASSWORD 'password';
```

### Create database:

```sql
CREATE DATABASE vectordb OWNER langchain;
```

### Grant privileges:

```sql
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE vectordb TO langchain;
```

---

## ⚙️ 4. Install pgvector

### Install dev package:

```bash
sudo apt install postgresql-server-dev-16
```

### Build pgvector:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector.git
cd pgvector

make clean
make PG_CONFIG=/usr/lib/postgresql/16/bin/pg_config
sudo make install PG_CONFIG=/usr/lib/postgresql/16/bin/pg_config
```

### Restart:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart postgresql
```

---

## 🧩 5. Enable pgvector Extension

```bash
psql -U postgres -h localhost -d vectordb
```

```sql
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;
\dx
```

👉 Confirms pgvector is installed.

---

## 🗄️ 6. Create Vector Table

```sql
CREATE TABLE documents (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    content TEXT,
    metadata JSONB,
    embedding VECTOR(384)
);
```

👉 `VECTOR(384)` = embedding size (depends on model)

---

## 📥 7. Insert Data

```sql
INSERT INTO documents (content, metadata, embedding)
VALUES (
    'LangChain is used for LLM apps',
    '{"source": "note1"}',
    '[0.1, 0.2, 0.3]'
);
```

---

## 🔍 8. Similarity Search

```sql
SELECT content,
       embedding <=> '[0.1, 0.2, 0.3]' AS distance
FROM documents
ORDER BY embedding <=> '[0.1, 0.2, 0.3]'
LIMIT 5;
```

### Operators:

* `<->` → Euclidean distance
* `<=>` → Cosine distance
* `<#>` → Inner product

---

## ⚡ 9. Create Index (for performance)

```sql
CREATE INDEX documents_embedding_idx
ON documents
USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops);
```

👉 Makes similarity search fast for large data.

